## Components (rebuilt, tasks 203–206)
- `src/memory/manager.rs` — `MemoryManager` orchestrator; `beliefs.json` is the ONE store (`BELIEFS_FILE`)
- `src/memory/mod.rs` — `MemoryHandle` (working memory)
- `src/memory/episodic.rs` — disk-backed event storage, fsynced (`HELIX_EPISODES_FILE`)
- `src/memory/vector.rs` — disk-backed vector facts with **real Ollama embeddings** (`HELIX_EMBED_URL`, `HELIX_EMBED_MODEL`, default `nomic-embed-text`); degrades honestly to keyword search when no embedder is reachable
- Nightly consolidation (task 205) — short-term → long-term path, runs via the cron registry

## Responsibilities
- Inject context into LLM prompts
- Store beliefs (`beliefs.json`, single source of truth)
- Provide short-term + long-term recall
- Persist across restarts (disk-backed episodic + vector)

## OKF knowledge (tasks 207–208)
- `src/okf/` — `OkfLibrarian`, `OkfFetcher`, `OkfRegistry`, `OkfValidator`, `OkfBundleManifest`
- Protocol contract: `PROTOCOL.md` (v1) — `/okf/manifest.json`, `/okf/bundles/{id}/manifest.json`, `/okf/knowledge/{kid}`, `POST /okf/traces` (flushed before the 202 ack), `POST /okf/bundles/{b}/concepts`
- Helix runs its own OKF server (`[helix.okf] enabled`, serves `/okf/*` on the web port, self-fetch via `server_url`)
- **Direction**: in-Helix server stays as the **offline fallback**; the Dell's shared OKF backend becomes primary (unification Phase 3)

